<p>Likutay
Moharan Volume 1: Torah 39</p>
<p>And I will give
grass in your field for your cattle. (Deuteronomy 11)</p>
<p>[In
the language of our master, of blessed memory]</p>
<p>Grass
initials make peace in His heights in your field, language of
plundering and breaking when a person feels some hunger, that the
desire of eating overcomes him know that he has enemies (see Bava
Metzia 59b) Who
sets peace in your border (Psalms
147) and one who has poor below, it is known that he has poor above
(Sanhedrin 103b) therefore one needs to plunder and break his
animality that desires to eat for the main of the hunger is to the
animality (Bereishit parsha 63) pride comes and disgrace comes, this
is the disgrace of hunger, as it is written (Ezekiel 36) Which
you shall no longer bear the disgrace of hunger among the nations it
turns out the dispute, that is what they disgrace a person comes
through this the aspect of hunger and this hunger, that is the aspect
of dispute, the aspect of disgrace, it is the aspect of foreskin as
it is written (Genesis 34): For
it is a disgrace to us and
the foreskin they are three shells, that surround the bris peace
and when they break the foreskin, then the bris peace
is revealed and when there is peace below, there is peace above in
His heights and when there is peace above, then great satiety is
revealed and increased in the world as it is written by Joseph (there
47): Give
seed and we shall live another
explanation (Job 5) And
your offspring like the grass of the earth in
your field for your cattle that is when will you have living and
enduring sons when your mating will be in holiness and you break your
desiring soul, that is the animal soul and it shall seem to you as if
you force a demon (Nedarim 20b) and this in your field, language of
demon through this you will have enduring sons for the death of sons,
this is because of the oppressed souls in the balance as known (see
Zohar Mishpatim 113a) for the balance, that is shells of nogah, it is
close to the animal soul, as brought (in Mishnat Chassidim in
tractate of composition). Also one needs that the main of your mating
be on Sabbath night that then it is included in holiness, and all
workers of iniquity separate from it and this And
you shall eat and be satisfied,
this hints on Sabbath that then the satiety from which the six days
are blessed.</p>
<p>Likutay
Moharan Volume 1: Torah 40</p>
<p>These are the
journeys of the children of Israel.</p>
<p>[In
the language of our master, of blessed memory]</p>
<p>It
is brought in the ten utterances: These are the journeys of the
children of Israel because they sinned in these are your gods Israel
because of this the children of Israel shall journey it turns out all
the journeys of a person, it is because of the spoiling of the faith
that is the aspect of idol worship for if he believed in complete
faith that the Holy One, blessed be He, can prepare for him all his
needs he would not journey any journey it turns out that the journey
is spoiling of faith, that is the aspect of idol worship and this
that is written in idol worship (Isaiah 30): Go
out say to him go
out, this is the aspect of journey and movement. Also through
movement he rectifies the movement that he caused as if above (there
28) And
the molten image is narrow as it gathers also
through idol worship, the rain is withheld as it is written
(Deuteronomy 11) And
you shall serve other gods etc. and there shall be no rain and
when there is no rain, there is no satiety (Psalms 72) The
mountains shall bear peace for the people,
as Rashi explained then no man helps his fellow and each one needs to
journey and move from place to place, for his sustenance also the
exile comes on the negation of Torah, as it is written (Isaiah 5): My
people are exiled for lack of knowledge and
through idol worship, comes withholding of rains and when there is no
flour, there is no Torah (Avot chapter 3).</p>
<p>Likutay
Moharan Volume 1: Torah 41</p>
<p>Dances</p>
<p>[In
the language of our master, of blessed memory]</p>
<p>Dances
behold it is brought (in Etz Chayim folio 22a) the knees that is the
legs, they are netzach hod, and they are heels and heel gematria two
times Elokim, which are judgments, that there is grasping there for
the externals as known and the action to drive away the externals
from there, that he draws into the knees, the strengths from the root
of understanding and when he draws the root of the strengths from
understanding, then the externals flee from there, and he takes the
birthright and the blessing, that this is the aspect of knees and the
root of the birthrights, is called wine as known and this is wine
that gladdens and this that is written by Jacob, when he saw that he
is the aspect of knees in the place of judgment for two times Elokim
with ten letters gematria Jacob then he drew the root of the
strengths, the aspect of wine that gladdens as it is written (Genesis
27): And
he brought him wine and he drank the
root of the blessing it turns out through dances, that drinks wine
that gladdens, which are the root of the strengths that are in the
understanding and are drawn below into the legs, that is that he
dances in this drives away the externals from there and this is the
flaming of the dance, and it is A
fire offering a pleasing aroma to Hashem (Numbers
28) but one who dances in flaming of the inclination this is called
the sin of Nadav and Avihu that it is written by them (Leviticus 10):
And they offered strange fire Nadav and Avihu, they are netzach and
hod and flaming that is in holiness, is called wine that gladdens,
that through it the birthrights are sweetened and strange fire, is
called wine that intoxicates, flaming of the inclination and there is
Heaven forbid grasping for the externals, which He did not command
them and this also is redemption of soul for the money is called
pillars, as it is written (Deuteronomy 11): And
the standing that is on their feet (Pesachim
119a) and when the tzadik who
does the redemption lays his hands on the money he should intend for
there is the great hand etc., and that is three hands and three times
yud gematria 42 and the name of 42 has seven names and each name has
six letters and he should intend to draw to him the vavs, that is the
seven names that each one has six letters to draw them into the money
which is called pillars and then it is called vavs of the pillars and
these pillars, that is legs that is heels, they are the aspect of
judgment for two times Elokim, gematria heel and there is grasping
there for the externals and judgment is not sweetened except in its
root and the root of the judgments in the understanding, as it is
written (in the Zohar Vayikra 10a): Understanding judgments are
aroused from it, I
am understanding power is mine (Proverbs
8) and the name of 42 in the understanding it turns out when he draws
the name of 42 into pillars then the judgments are sweetened in their
root (Exodus 27): Vavs
of the pillars and their fillets silver explanation:
through attachment and connection vavs with pillars, there is made
silver, kindness, that the judgments are sweetened Etz Chayim chapter
13 (hall of the crowns gate 1): Name of 42 in the understanding, and
these 42 they are 300 lights that illuminate 8 whiteness gematria in
peace (there in chapter 14) gematria chashmal garment, that this
chashmal guards upper garments from the moth of shell, as it is
written (Isaiah 51): Like
a garment the moth shall eat them and
this (Yoma 71b): One who wants to pour wine on the altar, let him
fill the throats of Torah scholars to pour, that is kingship and
dominion (Psalms 2): And
I have poured My king etc.
Wine, this is the aspect of understanding, root of the birthright
wine that gladdens altar this is the aspect of judgments Torah
scholars, they are the aspect of netzach hod and this is its
explanation: One who wants to make king and to rule and to sweeten
the judgments, through their root which is wine that gladdens what
shall he do, good advice: On this let him fill their throats, through
dances, or through redemption, as brought above also through filling
their throats, the judgments are sweetened (end of Berakhot): Torah
scholars increase peace in the world that through them the name of 42
is drawn, which are 300 lights, and with 8 whiteness, gematria in
peace and Torah scholars are called netzach hod, legs as brought in
the Midrash: His
legs pillars of marble they
are Torah scholars (see Targum) and also altar is called legs, as it
is written (Psalms 4): Sacrifice
sacrifices of righteousness,
and as it is written (there 85): Righteousness
shall go before Him and
this is the explanation (there 20) May
He give you according to your heart and
when, when And
all your counsel He will fulfill through
filling the throats of Torah scholars (Avot chapter 6): And they
enjoy from him counsel and wisdom and as it is written (there
33): The
counsel of Hashem stands forever that
they are pillars of the world (Isaiah 14) Hashem
of hosts has counseled,
Hashem of hosts, they are netzach and hod.</p>
<p>Likutay
Moharan Volume 1: Torah 42</p>
<p>And He saw their
distress when He heard their cry etc. (Psalms 106)</p>
<p>[In
the language of our master, of blessed memory]</p>
<p>Behold
through music, the judgments are sweetened as it is written in the
holy Zohar (Pinchas 215a) the bow it is the Shechinah and three
colors of the bow, they are the fathers, and they are garments of the
Shechinah and when it is clothed in garments of lights then And
I will see it to remember the everlasting covenant,
then and the wrath of the king subsided parable to a king who was
angry at his son and when the king sees the queen in garments of
lights then he has mercy on his son and letters of the prayer it is
the Shechinah, as it is written (Psalms 51): Adonai
open my lips that
the speech is the name Adonai and is called bow as Rashi explained
(Genesis 48): With
my sword and with my bow language
of prayer and the voice of the music they are three colors of the bow
that there are in the voice fire, water, wind, which are three
fathers that the fathers they are three colors of lights, in
which And
I will see it to remember etc.
it turns out one who plays the letters of the prayer and the voice of
the music they are in merit and in great brightness then he clothes
the Shechinah, that is the letters, in garments of lights and the
Holy One blessed be He sees it, then and the wrath of the king
subsided and this that Rashi explained When
He heard their cry in
the merit of the fathers that is when the music, which are three
colors of the bow as above, in brightness and in great merit for the
three colors they are the fathers as above and they are garments of
the Shechinah and when the garments are lights in merit and in
brightness, is called merit of the fathers then: And
I will see it to remember the everlasting covenant,
then: And
He relented according to the abundance of His kindness that
is: And the wrath of the king subsided, and the judgments are
sweetened also through faith in sages that he believes that all their
words and their deeds are not simple, and there are secrets in them
through this he clothes the bow in garments of lights then: And
I will see it to remember the everlasting covenant for
the tzadik is
the aspect of bow as Rabbi Shimon ben Yochai said to Rabbi Yehoshua
ben Levi: Was a bow seen in your days etc. (Ketubot 77b) and it is
brought in the holy Zohar (parsha Pinchas folio 215a): One whose
deeds to illuminate in them the Matronita and to strip from her
garments of darkness that she stripped and to adorn her in garments
of colors of secrets of the Torah what is written in it? And
I will see it to remember the everlasting covenant that
light secret is called and in that time anger rises from him and the
wrath of the king subsided also one who makes a fine garment for
the tzadik through
this the judgments are sweetened also this is aspects of blowings for
blowing shevarim teruah, they are the fathers Abraham Isaac Jacob and
your sign bow that is blowing etc. (Zohar parsha Pinchas 230a) and
this is (Job 22): And
the Almighty shall be in your distress for
the name Almighty they are the fathers (there 231a) for sh three
branches of the tree, which are the fathers and they are three names
of the unity, Hashem our G-d Hashem which are 14 letters, and they
are 14 of Almighty Abraham Isaac Jacob, they are the initials of
Hashem our G-d Hashem There
is no saying and there are no words without their voice being
heard (Psalms
19) this is the aspect of bow and voice, three colors of the bow.</p>
<p>Likutay
Moharan Volume 1: Torah 43</p>
<p>The speeches of
the wicked produce licentiousness in the hearer</p>
<p>[In
the language of our master, of blessed memory]</p>
<p>Know
that the speeches of the wicked who is a man of knowledge,
produce licentiousness in
the hearer for the matings are drawn from the knowledge as it is
written (Genesis 4): And
the man knew Eve his wife and
it is written (Numbers 31) Every
woman who has known a man but
there are two kinds of matings that is mating of holiness, it is
attachment to tzadikim,
and to the Torah, and to Hashem, blessed be He, this is drawn from
knowledge of holiness and matings of transgression, are drawn from
knowledge of shell and the speech is the revelation of the knowledge
for they do not know what is in the knowledge, except through the
speech as it is written (Psalms 19) And
night to night declares knowledge declares
from language of speech that the speech speaks what is in the
knowledge and when a wicked speaks and brings out from his mouth
vanities produces poisonous airs of licentiousness and
the hearer from him the speeches, and breathes breaths inserts into
his body these airs and therefore by Balaam who is aspects of
knowledge of shell as our sages expounded, of blessed memory (Sifri
parsha And this is the blessing, and in the Zohar Exodus 21b, Balak
193b): On the verse no one has arisen like Moses etc. in Israel no
one has arisen, but in the nations has arisen, and who Balaam
(Vayikra Rabbah 9) and therefore when Moab took counsel from Midian,
they said to them: His power is only in the mouth for the mouth is
the revelation of the knowledge Moab said also we will come upon them
with a man whose power is in the mouth (as brought in Rashi in parsha
Balak) for he also is knowledge of shell, as it is written
(Ecclesiastes 7): This
opposite this G-d made (Numbers
24): And
knows the knowledge of the Most High and
our rabbis expounded of blessed memory (Berakhot 7a): That he knew
when the Holy One blessed be He is angry for when the knowledge is
not in settlement, then there is anger as our rabbis said, of blessed
memory (Pesachim 66b): Anyone who is angry his wisdom departs from
him and therefore when Moses our master, peace be upon him, was angry
at the officers of the army when they came from Midian the knowledge
departed from him and Eleazar needed to say the laws of immersion of
vessels and when the knowledge is complete, then there is no anger,
as it is written (Isaiah 11): They
shall not hurt nor destroy in all My holy mountain for the earth
shall be full of knowledge and
Balaam was looking in knowledge of shell, which is the excesses of
upper knowledge and when it changes he knew that the Holy One blessed
be He is in anger it turns out that Balaam is knowledge of shell and
through his speeches he produced poisonous airs of licentiousness to
this when they came from the war of Midian, it is written (Numbers
31): And
Moses was angry with the officers of the army, and he said have you
kept every female alive, behold they were through the word of
Balaam through
the word precisely, for through his words, which is the revelation of
his knowledge, he produced licentiousness in
Midian and therefore when they came from the wars of Midian, it is
written (there): And
the heads of the officers approached Moses etc. and they said and we
have brought near the offering of Hashem etc., to atone for our souls
before Hashem and
our rabbis expounded, of blessed memory (Shabbat 64a): That thus they
said even though from the hands of transgression we came out, from
the hands of thought we did not come out.</p>
<p>Likutay
Moharan Volume 1: Torah 44</p>
<p>What one strikes
palm to palm at the time of prayer</p>
<p>[In
the language of our master, of blessed memory]</p>
<p>What
one strikes palm to palm at the time of prayer for our sages said, of
blessed memory (Bereishit Rabbah parsha 1): Why did the Torah begin
from Bereishit for the nations will say to us robbers you are, that
you conquered the land of seven nations because of this, the power of
His works He declared to His people that He declared that all the
worlds all are the works of His hands and to whom the Holy One
blessed be He wants He gives and this, to give them the inheritance
of nations, for in His hand all and all the things are called the
power of His works opposite 28 letters of the work of Bereishit,
opposite 28 joints of the hands and this is known that the air of the
land of the nations it is impure (see Shabbat 15b Gittin 8a Nazir 54a
55b) and the air of the land of Israel it is holy and pure for the
Holy One blessed be He took out from under the hand of the nations
and gave to us but the land of peoples, which is outside the land,
there air impure and when we clap palm to palm, in this 28 letters of
the work of Bereishit are aroused, the power of His works and it
turns out that in His hand to give us the inheritance of nations for
all is of the Holy One blessed be He and in this there is power in
our hand to purify the air of the land of the peoples for the land of
the peoples returns under the dominion of the Holy One blessed be He
and in His hand to give to whomever He wants, as it is written: To
give them the inheritance of nations and
then the air of the place where the Israelite man prays is purified
and he draws holy air like in the land of Israel. Also through
clapping of palm, the impure air is driven away for through [clapping
of] palms a voice is heard and this voice it is holy air from 28
letters of the work of Bereishit, from 28 joints of the hands as we
see in sense, that the air is driven away through clapping of palms
and because of this one needs to fix a place for his prayer (Berakhot
6b) as we see in sense, that people who come to a province that they
are not accustomed to its air through this they weaken and die even
from an evil abode to a beautiful abode (see Ketubot 110b) so the
matter in prayer even when he stands to pray in a place where
a tzadik prayed
nevertheless it is very hard for him to pray there for he is not
accustomed to the air of the place all the more from a beautiful
abode to an evil abode and this that our sages said, of blessed
memory (there): Anyone who fixes a place etc., the G-d of Abraham in
his help for through him the world is built anew and building of the
world through Abraham, as it is written (Psalms 89) A
world of kindness shall be built and
this that is brought in the Tikkunim Tikkun 22 (folio 66a) and with
this power Israel are strengthened over Edom. And further, (there):
One needs to raise this power to the side of wisdom and this is the
aspect of: Anyone who fixes a place for his prayer the G-d of Abraham
in his help for Abraham he is right, one who wants to become wise let
him go south (Bava Batra 25b) and further, the G-d of Abraham in his
help for Abraham he is first to the attainment of the land of Israel
as it is brought in the Zohar (Lech Lecha 78b) stumble in the balance
until it is revealed to him and this is the explanation, (Berakhot
26b): Prayers opposite the continual offerings they instituted
continual, this is aspects of the land of Israel (see Shocher Tov
Psalm 105 Deuteronomy 11) as it is written Continually
the eyes of Hashem your G-d are upon it that
is one needs to see that he pray his prayer in the air of the land of
Israel that is the rectification of foreign thoughts that are in the
prayer which they are aspects of prayers opposite as above their
rectification through continual, through aspects of the land of
Israel and this is the explanation, (Hosea 12): And
by the hand of the prophets I will be likened through
the hands, through clapping of palm, the speeches are spoken in the
land of holiness (Zechariah 2 Rashi Exodus 6 on And Aaron your
brother shall be your prophet). Also through clapping of palm,
killing and destruction are nullified from the world for the hands
they are aspects of: Let
there be light and there was light,
right and left and it is written (Genesis 1): And
G-d saw the light etc., and He separated between the light this
is Aaron (Tikkunim Tikkun 30 71b) and this is aspects of (Leviticus
26): And
I will give peace in the land and a sword shall not pass through your
land You
stand this day (Deuteronomy
29): There is no standing but prayer (Berakhot 6b) Before
Hashem your G-d this
is aspects of the land of Israel as our sages said of blessed memory
(Ketubot 110b): Anyone who dwells in the land of Israel is like one
who has a G-d that is through what will you merit that your prayer be
in the air of the land of Israel your heads your tribes etc., and
counts ten aspects, that is aspects of clapping of palm through
clapping of palms, the prayer is in the air of the land of Israel as
above. Prayers opposite continual offerings etc., that is aspects of
the land of Israel that is through clapping of palm, foreign thoughts
are nullified for anyone who dwells outside the land is like one who
has no G-d and anyone who dwells in the land of Israel is like one
who has a G-d and through clapping of palm then he dwells in the air
of the land of Israel and he has a G-d and foreign thoughts are
nullified (Exodus 17) And
his hands were faith until the sun came,
and its Targum: Spread in prayer and opposite faith, they are the
denials foreign thoughts of nations and their rectification through
continual offerings, through the land of Israel, through clapping of
palm and this is the explanation, (Isaiah 62): And
you shall be a crown of splendor in the hand of Hashem explanation:
Through the hand of Hashem, through clapping of palm that the hands
of the Holy One blessed be He are aroused as above through this the
thoughts of nations are rectified for through nations he damages in
splendor, as it is written (there 44): As
the splendor of a man to dwell in the house when
he rectifies his thoughts through this there is made a crown of
splendor that splendor is crowned with the crown that his mother
crowned him (Song of Songs 3) another explanation prayers opposite
that is the foreign thoughts which are opposite which confuse his
prayer and are called flood which confuse his prayer and their
rectification that he give charity to the land of Israel and through
this he is included in the land of Israel upon which it is said: A
land that is not rained upon on the day of wrath (as
our rabbis expounded of blessed memory Zevachim 113a) and through
this he is saved from foreign thoughts and this continual offerings
their institution, their rectification through the land of Israel
upon which it is said: A
land which etc. continually the eyes of Hashem your G-d are upon it.
Also the air of the land of Israel makes wise (Bava Batra 158b) and
through this the brain is purified, that is his thought (Genesis
9) And
I will see it to remember the everlasting covenant and
I will see it, through aspects of the land of Israel through this the
everlasting bris is
aroused and rectified aspects of prayer, 18 blessings of
prayer, tzadik lives
of worlds [all this matter from the beginning of sign 44 until here
is connected together. And so we heard many these things in one
exposition. But in his holy writing, he divided them a little and so
was his way several times, and I did not know his reason].</p>
<p>Likutay
Moharan Volume 1: Torah 45</p>
<p>Clapping of
palms in prayer</p>
<p>[In
the language of our master, of blessed memory]</p>
<p>Clapping
of palms at the time of prayer this is aspects of giving the bed
between north to south (Berakhot 5b) for bed that is aspects of
mating aspects of prayer (Tikkun 10 and see Tikkun 58) and north and
south, this is aspects of hands and this that Abba Binyamin prayed
(Berakhot 5b): That his prayer be close to his bed that is that there
be no separation between the prayer to the mating also through
clapping of palm, the judgments are sweetened for there are three
havayot, which are the aspect of three hands the great hand the
strong hand, the high hand and the right hand this is the great hand
and the left hand, this is the strong hand and at the time of
striking that they are connected together this is the aspect of high
hand and the speeches that come out, they come out from the throat
gematria three times Elokim and they are sweetened through three
havayot and this is the explanation (Psalms 119) My
soul in my palm continually etc.
My soul, this is aspects of speech (Song of Songs 5) My
soul went out when he spoke in
my palm continually, that is when he strikes palm to palm at the time
of the prayer through this, And
Your Torah I have not forgotten,
initials shalav gematria three havayot and three Elokim, that is the
sweetening of the judgments. Also, the main forgetfulness is from
brains of smallness, from aspects of Elokim and when he sweetens the
judgments as above, then he is in brains of greatness, and he has no
forgetfulness and Your Torah I have not forgotten, initials shalav
that is through that he sweetens three Elokim, in three havayot as
above, he has no forgetfulness and this precisely at the time of the
prayer for then he knows if he is in brains of smallness, or of
greatness for the speech is the revelation of the brains as it is
written (Proverbs 2): From
His mouth knowledge and understanding.</p>
<p>Likutay
Moharan Volume 1: Torah 46</p>
<p>Clapping of palm
at the time of prayer</p>
<p>[In
the language of our master, of blessed memory]</p>
<p>Clapping
of palm at the time of the prayer this is aspects of arousal of
